{"book":"functions","bookTitle":"Functions and relationships","concept":2,"title":"Input and output","grades":"Grade 5","goal":"I can use a flow diagram to find outputs from inputs.","teach":"A <b>flow diagram</b> takes an <b>input</b> number, does one or more operations in order, and gives an <b>output</b>. Follow the arrows: do the first operation, then the next.","tvis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:356px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 274 120\"><rect x=\"4.0\" y=\"4.0\" width=\"54.0\" height=\"112.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"31.0\" y=\"26.2\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">1</text><text x=\"31.0\" y=\"52.2\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">2</text><text x=\"31.0\" y=\"78.2\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">3</text><text x=\"31.0\" y=\"104.2\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">4</text><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"60.0\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M74,55.0 L81,60.0 L74,65.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><rect x=\"84\" y=\"44.0\" width=\"40\" height=\"32\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"104.0\" y=\"65.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">× 3</text><line x1=\"126\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"146\" y2=\"60.0\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M140,55.0 L147,60.0 L140,65.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"44.0\" width=\"40\" height=\"32\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"170.0\" y=\"65.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">+ 2</text><line x1=\"192\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"212\" y2=\"60.0\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M206,55.0 L213,60.0 L206,65.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><rect x=\"216.0\" y=\"4.0\" width=\"54.0\" height=\"112.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"243.0\" y=\"26.2\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">5</text><text x=\"243.0\" y=\"52.2\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">8</text><text x=\"243.0\" y=\"78.2\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">11</text><text x=\"243.0\" y=\"104.2\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">14</text></svg></span><div class=\"cap\">Each input is multiplied by 3, then 2 is added.</div></div>","ex":{"q":"The input 7 goes through “× 3, then + 2”. What is the output?","steps":["First operation: 7 × 3 = 21.","Second operation: 21 + 2 = 23.","The output is 23."]},"watch":"Follow the order of the arrows. For the input 7 and “× 3, then + 2”, the output is 7 × 3 + 2 = 23. If you add 2 first, you get (7 + 2) × 3 = 27, which is wrong.","qs":[{"text":"The machine multiplies by 5. The output is 50. What was the input?","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Input","a":"10","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"50 ÷ 5","steps":"1. Rule (inverse): to work backwards, undo the last step first (− undoes +, ÷ undoes ×).<br>2. The machine does × 5.<br>3. Undo × 5: 50 ÷ 5 = 10<br>4. input = 10"},{"text":"Find the output. First multiply by 4, then subtract 3.","vis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:356px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 274 42\"><rect x=\"4.0\" y=\"4.0\" width=\"54.0\" height=\"34.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"31.0\" y=\"26.2\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">5</text><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"21.0\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"21.0\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M74,16.0 L81,21.0 L74,26.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><rect x=\"84\" y=\"5.0\" width=\"40\" height=\"32\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"104.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">× 4</text><line x1=\"126\" y1=\"21.0\" x2=\"146\" y2=\"21.0\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M140,16.0 L147,21.0 L140,26.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"5.0\" width=\"40\" height=\"32\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"170.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">− 3</text><line x1=\"192\" y1=\"21.0\" x2=\"212\" y2=\"21.0\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M206,16.0 L213,21.0 L206,26.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><rect x=\"216.0\" y=\"4.0\" width=\"54.0\" height=\"34.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"226\" y1=\"28.2\" x2=\"260\" y2=\"28.2\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/></svg></span></div>","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Output","a":"17","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"5 × 4, then − 3.","steps":"1. Rule (flow diagram): do the operations in the order of the arrows, one at a time.<br>2. input = 5<br>3. 5 × 4 = 20<br>4. 20 − 3 = 17"},{"text":"At the tuck shop, the price is the number of muffins × R9. What do 7 muffins cost?","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Cost (rand)","a":"63","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"7 × 9","steps":"1. Formula: total = rate × number of units + fixed amount.<br>2. price = number of muffins × R9<br>3. = 7 × 9<br>4. = R63"}]}